1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,539
A child rides down a slide.

2
00:00:02,539 --> 00:00:04,244
Rain runs off a roof.

3
00:00:04,244 --> 00:00:05,992
A truck rolls downhill.

4
00:00:06,392 --> 00:00:08,696
Gravity pulls each one straight down.

5
00:00:08,696 --> 00:00:10,823
Yet they all move along a slope.

6
00:00:11,273 --> 00:00:15,394
Aarav stops pedalling at the top of
the college road, and coasts down.

7
00:00:15,744 --> 00:00:18,754
He speeds up, but far
slower than a falling stone.

8
00:00:18,754 --> 00:00:20,054
What holds him back?

9
00:00:20,554 --> 00:00:23,250
The answer is one simple
split of his weight.

10
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:28,847
An inclined plane is a flat surface,
tilted at an angle theta to the ground.

11
00:00:29,197 --> 00:00:33,135
A block on it feels its weight from
the Earth, and the normal force from

12
00:00:33,135 --> 00:00:34,035
the slope.

13
00:00:34,271 --> 00:00:37,748
On a rough slope, it also feels
friction, along the slope.

14
00:00:38,148 --> 00:00:39,652
To the motion notebook.

15
00:00:39,652 --> 00:00:42,907
A block on a smooth slope,
tilted to thirty degrees.

16
00:00:43,257 --> 00:00:45,980
Its weight, m g, pulls straight down.

17
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:46,880
Let go.

18
00:00:46,701 --> 00:00:48,803
It slides, faster and faster.

19
00:00:49,203 --> 00:00:50,270
Slow-mo replay.

20
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:52,214
Freeze, and tilt the axes.

21
00:00:52,214 --> 00:00:54,427
x along the slope, y into it.

22
00:00:54,827 --> 00:00:57,090
Into the slope: m g cos theta.

23
00:00:57,090 --> 00:01:00,222
The slope pushes back
with N, so they cancel.

24
00:01:00,622 --> 00:01:02,874
Along the slope: m g sine theta.

25
00:01:02,874 --> 00:01:05,706
Nothing cancels it, so
the block speeds up.

26
00:01:06,106 --> 00:01:07,531
a is g sine theta.

27
00:01:07,531 --> 00:01:12,228
Nine point eight times a half: four
point nine metres per second squared.

28
00:01:12,828 --> 00:01:14,498
Tilt it to sixty degrees.

29
00:01:14,498 --> 00:01:16,652
a jumps to eight point four nine.

30
00:01:17,052 --> 00:01:18,304
Tilt it to ten.

31
00:01:18,304 --> 00:01:19,859
Only one point seven.

32
00:01:20,259 --> 00:01:22,822
On the graph, a follows a sine curve.

33
00:01:22,822 --> 00:01:24,744
At ninety degrees, a is g.

34
00:01:24,744 --> 00:01:25,644
Free fall.

35
00:01:26,176 --> 00:01:27,526
Now make it rough.

36
00:01:27,526 --> 00:01:29,274
Mu k, zero point three.

37
00:01:29,274 --> 00:01:32,509
Friction points up the
slope, against the sliding.

38
00:01:32,909 --> 00:01:36,235
At thirty degrees, a drops
to two point three five.

39
00:01:36,235 --> 00:01:38,041
The rough curve sits below.

40
00:01:38,691 --> 00:01:40,818
Now the rule, one step at a time.

41
00:01:41,168 --> 00:01:42,068
Step one.

42
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:43,291
Tilt the axes.

43
00:01:43,291 --> 00:01:48,572
The weight splits: m g sine theta
along, m g cos theta into the slope.

44
00:01:49,322 --> 00:01:50,240
Step two.

45
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,757
Across the slope, nothing moves.

46
00:01:52,757 --> 00:01:54,961
So N equals m g cos theta.

47
00:01:55,711 --> 00:01:56,742
Step three.

48
00:01:56,742 --> 00:01:59,983
Smooth slope: m g sine theta equals m a.

49
00:01:59,983 --> 00:02:02,069
So a equals g sine theta.

50
00:02:02,819 --> 00:02:03,748
Step four.

51
00:02:03,748 --> 00:02:07,636
Rough, sliding down:
friction, mu k N, points up.

52
00:02:07,636 --> 00:02:11,385
a equals g, times sine
theta minus mu k cos theta.

53
00:02:12,135 --> 00:02:13,100
Step five.

54
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,651
Sliding up, friction points down.

55
00:02:15,651 --> 00:02:19,722
It slows at g, times sine
theta plus mu k cos theta.

56
00:02:20,472 --> 00:02:21,541
Remember this.

57
00:02:21,541 --> 00:02:24,627
Along a slope, gravity
is only g sine theta.

58
00:02:24,627 --> 00:02:27,183
And friction always fights the sliding.

59
00:02:27,883 --> 00:02:29,698
Notice: the mass cancelled.

60
00:02:29,698 --> 00:02:30,598
Why?

61
00:02:30,175 --> 00:02:31,186
Link by link.

62
00:02:31,536 --> 00:02:34,556
Double the mass, and the
pull along the slope doubles.

63
00:02:34,956 --> 00:02:38,670
But twice the mass also needs
twice the force to speed up.

64
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:40,245
The two cancel.

65
00:02:40,245 --> 00:02:43,781
A heavy suitcase and a light
book slide down together.

66
00:02:44,431 --> 00:02:47,222
Side by side, on a rough
thirty degree slope.

67
00:02:47,222 --> 00:02:49,141
Left: the block is pushed up.

68
00:02:49,541 --> 00:02:52,448
Gravity's part and
friction both point down.

69
00:02:52,448 --> 00:02:54,891
It slows at seven point four five.

70
00:02:55,291 --> 00:02:56,930
Right: it slides down.

71
00:02:56,930 --> 00:02:58,520
Friction points up now.

72
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:01,323
It speeds up at only two point three five.

73
00:03:01,923 --> 00:03:02,960
Now you try.

74
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:05,909
It goes up, stops, and slides back down.

75
00:03:05,909 --> 00:03:07,611
Which trip takes longer?

76
00:03:07,611 --> 00:03:08,899
Pause and decide.

77
00:03:12,099 --> 00:03:13,244
The trip down!

78
00:03:13,244 --> 00:03:16,090
Same distance, but a smaller acceleration.

79
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,753
Another pair.

80
00:03:17,753 --> 00:03:21,170
Two smooth slopes, both
two point five metres high.

81
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:23,047
Thirty degrees, and sixty.

82
00:03:23,447 --> 00:03:24,347
Race them.

83
00:03:24,346 --> 00:03:25,834
The steep one wins.

84
00:03:25,834 --> 00:03:29,864
Zero point eight two seconds,
against one point four three.

85
00:03:30,464 --> 00:03:31,364
Your turn.

86
00:03:31,346 --> 00:03:34,265
Which block is moving
faster at the bottom?

87
00:03:34,265 --> 00:03:35,562
Pause and decide.

88
00:03:38,762 --> 00:03:39,662
The same!

89
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:41,357
Seven metres per second.

90
00:03:41,357 --> 00:03:45,142
The gentle slope gives a
smaller a, but a longer run.

91
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:47,344
And a times L is always g h.

92
00:03:47,994 --> 00:03:49,729
Now, one worked example.

93
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:53,135
A ramp five metres long
rises three metres.

94
00:03:53,135 --> 00:03:56,807
A box slides from rest,
mu k zero point two five.

95
00:03:56,807 --> 00:03:58,664
Find its speed and time.

96
00:03:59,164 --> 00:04:02,498
Sine theta is three over
five, zero point six.

97
00:04:02,498 --> 00:04:04,922
So cos theta is zero point eight.

98
00:04:05,672 --> 00:04:10,475
a equals nine point eight, times
zero point six minus zero point two.

99
00:04:10,475 --> 00:04:12,090
Three point nine two.

100
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,544
v squared is two a L.

101
00:04:14,544 --> 00:04:17,448
Two times three point nine two times five.

102
00:04:17,448 --> 00:04:19,839
So v is about six point two six.

103
00:04:20,589 --> 00:04:22,443
The time is v over a.

104
00:04:22,443 --> 00:04:24,968
About one point six zero seconds.

105
00:04:25,618 --> 00:04:27,083
Now, the exam trap.

106
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:31,069
Many students use the minus
sign for a block sliding up.

107
00:04:31,469 --> 00:04:33,572
But friction opposes the sliding.

108
00:04:33,572 --> 00:04:35,980
Going up, it points down the slope.

109
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:38,704
So it is sine theta plus mu k cos theta.

110
00:04:39,354 --> 00:04:40,834
Where is this asked?

111
00:04:40,834 --> 00:04:45,074
In slope numericals: find a,
the time, the speed, or mu k.

112
00:04:45,674 --> 00:04:46,878
Exam level now.

113
00:04:46,878 --> 00:04:51,706
A block slides from rest down a smooth
thirty seven degree incline, reaching

114
00:04:51,706 --> 00:04:53,329
six metres per second.

115
00:04:53,329 --> 00:04:58,596
Made rough, with mu k zero point five,
what is its new speed at the bottom?

116
00:04:58,596 --> 00:04:59,852
Pause and solve.

117
00:05:05,252 --> 00:05:06,567
The answer is B.

118
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:08,869
Two root three metres per second.

119
00:05:09,369 --> 00:05:11,457
Smooth: a is point six g.

120
00:05:11,457 --> 00:05:14,024
Rough: point six minus point four.

121
00:05:14,024 --> 00:05:15,451
Just point two g.

122
00:05:15,951 --> 00:05:18,444
Same length, so v squared follows a.

123
00:05:18,444 --> 00:05:20,151
The new a is one third.

124
00:05:20,651 --> 00:05:22,693
So v is six over root three.

125
00:05:22,693 --> 00:05:25,633
Two root three, about
three point four six.

126
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:27,693
Here is your recap.

127
00:05:27,693 --> 00:05:29,194
Screenshot this card.

128
00:05:32,394 --> 00:05:34,325
Can you answer these without help?

129
00:05:34,725 --> 00:05:35,625
One.

130
00:05:35,224 --> 00:05:39,368
Why does a heavy block not slide
down a smooth slope any faster?

131
00:05:40,268 --> 00:05:41,168
Two.

132
00:05:40,752 --> 00:05:44,519
Why does friction add to the
slowing when a block slides up?

133
00:05:45,419 --> 00:05:46,319
Three.

134
00:05:45,968 --> 00:05:49,310
On a smooth thirty degree
slope, what is a, and why?

135
00:05:50,410 --> 00:05:53,499
Next time: a falling bag drags a trolley.

136
00:05:53,499 --> 00:05:54,399
How fast?

137
00:05:54,378 --> 00:05:56,898
Connected bodies and pulley systems.
